{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1460568-gangrel-clan-meetings","id":1460568,"title":"Gangrel Clan Meetings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-20T12:28:08-07:00","id":1460568,"title":"Gangrel Clan Meetings","content":"Through some interesting curve balls players throw at me I\u2019m now at a point where a Gangrel fledgling who\u2019s wet behind the ears is planning to call a \u201cThing\u201d or \u201cGather\u201d. <br /> <br /> However in the current setting the primogen is incarcerated. The clans territory has been rescinded by the prince due to reports of garou in the area. The whip is reluctant to take the reins. An elder who is eligible would rather be an autarkis. Everyone else is too rag tag to take control but maybe he\u2019s planning on it. All the NPCs are in disarray. Idk. He could be winging it. <br /> <br /> How should I roleplay the pecking order they establish? It\u2019s supposed to last for days normally but with the time crunch the players are in I\u2019m unsure if this is feasible. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m apt to let him try. It\u2019s great to show the worlds nuance happenings but I want to portray it right and keep it fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T12:29:45-07:00","id":1460569,"title":"","content":"A worse thought ran through my mind is someone turns that meeting to a \u201cRevel\u201d as response to the shit show they\u2019ve suffered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T13:04:32-07:00","id":1460574,"title":"","content":"Why would anyone show up to the &quot;call&quot; of an unimportant and non-influential fledgling?<br /> <br /> Have no one show up other than some other equally unimportant young Gangrel, and then have him slink off once he realizes how embarrassing the situation is. At least then you can have some PC to NPC conversation, and you can drop any needed exposition and have some RP at least.<br /> <br /> Then at some point later, have some older neonate or young ancilla bump into the fledgling and have him explain how Gathers actually work. IMO, they're either set in advance in time or place by the elders to allow the clan's voice to be heard, or called in emergencies by influential elders to warn people of danger or try to win support for one of their schemes. But however you decide it in your chronicles, you can explain it. Maybe it's friendly advice to guide and encourage the PC. Maybe it's just disgruntled annoyance a the &quot;kid&quot; who needs a lesson. Maybe it's a warning by someone angry at the PC's presumption, and it's a dressing down. Whatever works for you. Maybe he gets multiple conversations of different types.<br /> <br /> Then at some point later in the chronicle, when a more powerful and influential Gangrel elder is ready for a Gather, he calls it and most of the NPCs show up for that. Because they are all interested in what that guy has to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T13:05:32-07:00","id":1460575,"title":"","content":"What goal does the PC want to achieve by &quot;taking control&quot; of the clan? Get their clanmates to rescue the primogen? Deal with the werewolves? Collectively get the prince to return their territory?<br /> <br /> That aside, <b>how is the fledgling calling the gather? </b>That's a question of both logistics and social issues. Like, does he have phone numbers for all his clanmates? Does he know where to physically find them himself/through ghoul or animal messengers? Lot more Gangrel exist &quot;off-grid&quot; than Ventrue and may not be easy to find. A wet-behind-the-ears Gangrel probably doesn't have contact info for all of the clan.<br /> <br /> This is also why things (and social gatherings in general) tend to be called in advance... you not only need time to get the word out, people need time to work the event into their schedules. Any Gangrel who tries to call a thing under a major time crunch is probably screwed.<br /> <br /> Next, <b>how many clanmates will actually attend?</b> If he's wet behind the ears, he probably doesn't have the social clout to call a big thing and expect everyone to show up. If a ten-year-old kid tries to get a bunch of grown-ups to come meet over something, he's pretty likely to get brushed off completely by a lot of them.<br /> <br /> The clan being in such dire straits works in the PC's favor, and should make his clanmates more inclined to hold an &quot;emergency meeting&quot;. But many of them may tell him to fuck off anyway. Don't expect a full guest list.<br /> <br /> If the PC is smart, though I wouldn't tell the player to do this OOC (coming up with good tactics is a player's job), they should approach the most respected available Gangrel, sell them on the idea of the thing, then approach other clanmates in their name. Pitch it as their idea rather than yours and you'll probably get more attendees.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>'s ideas here are also pretty great.<br /> <br /> <b>When and if the thing happens,</b> the Gangrel establish pecking order through (probably) fighting and other direct physical contests. Even a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Matasuntha_(VTM)\" target=\"_blank\">Gangrel methuselah</a> still has to do that. I'd also run a thing to include boasting and tale-telling (oral storytelling is a big part of Gangrel culture), plus other contests like hunting Lupines or deadly animals, feats of endurance (who can take a beating the longest before succumbing to torpor), aerial races in bird form, demonstrating whose command over animals is greatest (ordering as many animals as you can to perform feats as complex as you can), etc. Could be a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> The PC should have opportunities to prove they're not so wet behind the ears, and if they acquit themselves well, increase their social clout among the clan. The PC probably isn't going to establish themselves as the biggest baddest Gangrel in the area, but they don't necessarily <i>need</i> to. If you have something you want the clan to do, just sell the idea to whoever wins the initial dominance contests. Acquit yourself well over the next few nights and selling them on the idea will probably be easier, too.<br /> <br /> <b>If there's a big enough time crunch,</b> though, a more time-efficient alternative to a thing might just be approaching individual clanmates and asking for help with issues X and Y. Could be asking the autarkis to step up for a brief period and then step down. Could be convincing the whip he should take the reins. Depends what the PC is after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 09-20-2021, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T16:28:10-07:00","id":1460591,"title":"","content":"I do think that, <u><b>if</b></u> the clan is in a dire enough situation, and <u><b>if</b></u> no one among the obvious callers want to be the face of this stint, then the PC have a chance.<br /> <br /> Those two <u><b>if</b></u>s mean that his betters in the clan both recognize that the Gather is needed, but don't want to call it themselves.<br /> <br /> So if this really works, it means the PC have both a great opportunity but is also pretty much screwed. Better to be able to deal with a lot of pressure, put a good show when establishing the pecking order, and be prepared to deal with whatever not even the elders want to deal with.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the pecking order is pretty much straightforward. Impress others showing off your might in some, any, way. And let things sit in as everyone more or less decides who they're afraid off or at least can respect and who they're not going to hear BS from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}